meta {
  name: Get Section Question
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/assessments/attempts/{{assessmentAttemptId}}/sections/{{assessmentSectionIdVerbal}}/questions?question_order=1
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  question_order: 1
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Returns ONE question at a time, not the whole section's list — matches
  a "one question per screen, Next/Previous button" take-test UI.
  `question_order` (1-based, query param, defaults to 1) selects which
  question in the section to return.

  Response: `{ question, questionOrder, totalQuestions, hasNext,
  hasPrevious }`. `question.content` — content only, no `answer_key`
  ever included. `question.responseFormat` (e.g. "single_choice",
  "voice_mcq", "fill_blank_dropdown") tells the client which answer
  widget to render. `question.myAnswer` reflects any prior save for
  that question (null if never touched) — response, is_flagged,
  answered_at.

  To move to the next question: re-call with `question_order + 1` (use
  the response's own `hasNext` to know whether to show a "Next" button).
  404 "Question not found" if `question_order` is out of range for this
  section.
}
